*******************************************************************               Copyright (c) 1988*               Apple Computer, Inc.*               All rights reserved.********************************************************************               AppleDisk 3.5 Driver Version 0.02e01** NOTE:         This driver must be installed on the boot*               volume in the subdirectory "/SYSTEM/DRIVERS'.*               Additionally, the FileType for the driver file*               must be set to $00BB.  AuxType is also critical*               to the operating system recognizing the driver*               as a GS/OS device driver.  The AuxType is a long*               word which must have the upper word set to $0000.*               The most significant byte of the least significant*               word in the AuxType must be set to $01 to indicate*               an active GS/OS device driver or $81 to indicate*               an inactive GS/OS device driver.  The least*               significant byte of the least significant word*               of the AuxType field indicates the number of*               devices supported by the driver file.  This value*               should be analogous to the number of DIB's*               contained in the driver file.  GS/OS will only*               install the number of devices indicated in the*               AuxType field.**               GS/OS Device Driver:    FileType = $00BB*                                       AuxType  = $000001XX where:*                                                  XX = number of devices.**               An AuxType of $00000102 indicates two devices.  When*               building a device driver, the best way to set the*               FileType and AuxType is to use the Exerciser to get*               the current file info (GET_FILE_INFO), modify the*               FileType & AuxType and then SET_FILE_INFO.******************************************************************** REVISION HISTORY:** Date_____ Version By____ 	Description__________________________** 03-Mar-88 0.00e01 GA/RBM 	Started initial coding.** 07-Mar-88 0.00e02 rt/fb  	fix format call by storing original read_data*                          	hooks before this call or system will use patch*                          	incorrectly.** 08-Mar-88 0.00e03 RBM    	Startup now sets interleave itself and*                          	no longer calls generated startup.*                          	Shutdown sets 4:1 interleave.** 18-Mar-88 0.05a01 RBM    	DRVR_BUSY error will be returned on shutdown*                          	for all but last device.** 18-May-88 0.08a01 GA     	Fixed bug which causes stack crawl and crash*                          	if a bad disk is inserted into the drive.*                          	during a block read call.** 05-Jun-88 0.09a01 RBM    	Both write and read check the block size for*                          	a value of $0200 or $020C before passing off*                          	to the generated core routines.  An invalid*                          	parameter error will be returned for non-*                          	standard block sizes.** 08-Jun-88 0.09a02 RBM    	Post process all status calls with a status*                          	code of $0000 so that when media is ejected*                          	the status indicates offline and disk switch*                          	only on the first status call.  On subsequent*                          	status calls when the media is offline, only*                          	the offline will be indicated.** 23-Jun-88 0.09a03 RBM    	Added patch to firmware (VECTOR) to detect*                          	any direct firmware access by an application.*                          	Any direct access will result in the cache*                          	being flushed and VCRs marked as switched.*                          	Additionally, read, write & format will*                          	return a disk switch error while status call*                          	$0000 will return a disk switched status.**                          	Startup revised to use class 1 calls and*                          	then update the DIB class after the DIBs*                          	have been created.  Neccessary to accomodate*                          	status of class 1 devices.** 13-Jul-88 0.10a02 RBM    	Dispatch routine only checks for external access*                          	if the current call is not a startup.**                          	After detecting an external access, the dispatch*                          	routine will reinstall the hooks for patches that*                          	were installed at startup time.*** 15-Jul-88 0.10a03 RBM    	Disk switch history now uses the DIB_HW_UNIT*                          	to index into the status history list.*                          	Format options no longer specifies a linkref*                          	for format option #1.** 02-Aug-88 0.16b01 MSA/GRT	if error during format do NOT change default option*                          	changed appledisk3.5/control subroutine 'format'** 11-Aug88  0.17b01	RBM	changed appledisk3.5/control subroutine set_option*                       	set proper unit number in parameter list.** 02 Dec 88  4.1 a01	RBM	Ported device specific hardware access routines from* 				the generated driver core routines.** 21 Dec 88  4.1 d10	RBM	Add support for 10 speed rom.  The status call in the*				firmware cannot support GS/OS at the current time.  The*				loaded driver must therefore be modified so that the *				mergeit patch is not installed when running with a 10*				speed rom.  All other loaded driver operation shall *				remain the same.** 09 Jan 88		RBM	Access detect now returns to ROM dispatch table via RTL.** 31 Jan 89	2.1a01	RBM	Clear out SmartPort type/subtype during startup prior to*				issuing call to device (Chinook does not return an error*				on extended status call so status result remained from*				previous device).** 06 Feb 89	2.1a02	RBM	Startup call now checks $CnFB.  If extended SmartPort*				is not supported then the device driver will not be*				installed by GS/OS.** 26 Feb 89	2.1a03  RBM	Changed two Longa offs to longa ons at end of Shutdn.*				Problem noticed when system loader hung on bad id's** 27 Feb 89	2.1a04  JOA	Started modification to include direct read code and*				Multi-block 1:1 track read logic in to the ReadBlock*				function.  Requires 1K of space in Bank 01 for the*   				direct readdata routine plus about 2K more code size.* 20 Mar 89	2.1a04	JOA	Fixed the failure to check for a zero request count** 20 Mar 89	2.1a04	JOA	Fixed Reading of 524 byte blocks and call the* 				SmartPort ReadBytes call instead of the ReadBlock call** 23 Mar 89	2.1a04	JOA	Fixed the ShutDown call to properly reset firmware*				interleave to $04 and make the driver restartable** 24 Mar 89	3.0b01	JOA	Modified ReadTrack and Seek to enable interrupts*				once each time seek must move the head to a new cylindr** 30 Aug 91		JOA	Begin modifications to support NuMustang and FDHD drives*				Heavy mods to Startup to support 8 DIB's and scan the*				the slots for external slot NuMustang cards.** 09 Sep 91	4.0d00	JOA	Initial operational version for all the stuff except*				Get&SetFmtOptions Status&Control calls.** 13 Sep 91	4.0a01	JOA	Initial SCM release to testing with all functions.*				(Alpha Candidate)** 19 Sep 91	4.1a01	JOA	Initial version of driver for GS/OS 6.0 with Scatter*				Read firmware in Mustang and Driver Multi-block read*				support for NuMustang. (Using condiditonal assembly*				switch in the source code named "Version6x")** 17 Sep 91	4.0a02	JOA	Fixed bug in Startup that was using Y reg instead of*				a work variable to test for slot internal/external state** 24 Sep 91	4.0a03	JOA	Fixed another place in Startup that was still using Y*				instead of the new work variable SlotsReg.** 15 Jan 92	4.0a04	GAB	Added logic in Shutdown to effectively remove the*				external access notification code that is downloaded*				to Mustang during Startup.** 24 Jan 92	4.0a05	GAB	A READ request with a combination of starting block*				and request count which would read >= 5 blocks but*				read beyond the end of the volume would return with*				no error and the transfer count equal to the request*				count as if the read completed without error.  In*				the multiblock read logic, the driver is correctly*				limiting the read to the remainder of the blocks in*				the volume, but is not limiting the request count*				at the same time.  In addition, the drvr_bad_block*				error was placed in the accumulator, but the carry*				was not being set.  This has all been corrected.**************************************************************************************** 3-Jun-92	5.4a01	DAL	AD3.5.main no longer crams 'A', 'B', etc onto*				device names during a warm start.  So you can*				rename your 3.5 devices and not have the names*				mutilated on return from P8.**************************************************************************************